OL,3,A'Silence is complicity' - top
OL,4,Afootballer hits out over Cameroon
OL,5,Afemicides
OL,6,
OL,7,FThe killing of at least eight women in
OL,8,Fa week has sparked outrage in Cameroon,
OL,9,Fwith many calling on the government to
OL,10,Fdo more to protect women and girls.
OL,12,FAmong those who have spoken out is
OL,13,Frenowned footballer Nchout Njoya Ajara,
OL,14,Fwho has called for an end to the
OL,15,F"tragic wave" of targeting women,
OL,16,Fsaying "silence is complicity".
OL,23,APub: 27-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,320,300,200,140,0,100
